  "behavior": [
    "One native conditional batch commits the slot claim, account count, and retained history marker.",
    "Claims bind account, gateway job ID, work kind, and selected bound. Exact reserve and release retries preserve counts.",
    "A released claim cannot be reserved again. A missing claim cannot release any capacity.",
    "Both videos and batches use the same account count and persist distinct claim IDs before dispatch. The HTTP fixture inspects actual claim ownership.",
    "Video release retries independently of optional accounting. A lost release acknowledgement or job stamp cannot free another job.",
    "Batch cancellation retains capacity until admitted lines drain. Durable RunFinished state permits later reads to recover release after restart.",
    "Batch updates bind the complete caller-observed record. Stale updates cannot erase ownership completion.",
    "Schema 2 job and batch records fence older readers. Versioned values at the old counter key make legacy scalar increments and decrements fail.",
    "Legacy scalar counts, unsupported schemas, and retained claims with missing count or history require recovery. The video API maps unknown ownership to a retryable 503.",
    "Follow-up f5788320 bounds the deferred batch cleanup read to five seconds. The focused race suite passes 156 results on this final source."
  ],
